<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 95,000 -USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 95,000 -USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts were :</p>
<p>Thursday: 95,000  Wk ago: 102,000  Yr ago: Holiday</p>
<p>Friday:  Holiday  Wk ago:  92,000  Yr ago: 96,000</p>
<p>Saturday: 5,000   Wk ago:   9,000  Yr ago: 14,000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were $1.00 per cwt lower than the midsession Wednesday. Trade slow for light demand, offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    57.50 -58.50	   58.50 -59.50</p>
<p>few				 59.00		    60.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    56.50 -58.50	   57.00 -59.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    56.50 -58.50	   57.00 -59.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 4.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs   41.00 -45.00	   41.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -46.50	   44.00 -46.50</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    45.00 -48.00	   46.00 -48.00</p>
<p>Compared to last week: Barrows and Gilts steady. Sows steady to 3.00 lower.  Receipts this week 418,000 last week 511,000, last year 403,000.  Barrows and Gilts average weight for week ending June 28, 1997  2 52.1 lbs compared to 253.0 lbs previous week 247.0 lbs last year.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
